  "overview": "Jarmusch told The Playlist that he was preparing to shoot his next film — and, in a surprising twist for the director and Sqürl collaborator, the new film may feature no music whatsoever. “The film we’re preparing now for late this year to shoot, probably, I think, may have no music,” he explained. “It’s a very subtle film; it’s very quiet. And I think music could move it too much one way — it’s a funny and sad film, right? It sort of has both woven in. I don’t know if I wanna have music to add some other thing over it. It doesn’t really want it so far.” Exoskeleton an emerging production company is reportedly developing a new project titled as, ‘Father Mother Sister Brother’. Being a relatively new production company, Exoskeleton will be teaming up with Animal Kingdom and CG Cinéma for the upcoming feature film. Animal Kingdom is a production company based in New York. CG Cinéma is another production company which is based in Paris. The upcoming movie has supposedly commenced its filming in November 2023 and is predicted to complete its production in March 2024. West Milford, New Jersey and Paris, France will be serving as the primary locations for ‘Father Mother Sister Brother’.",
